# Pairs with BackupSagaConsistent, and reproduces production before the #4619 fix.
# TxRegistryGrain.CaptureLocalDecisions reported an expired decision tombstone
# whose row is still stored as Indeterminate, so the capture hides the key of
# a pending bucket, while the sweeps apply the recorded verdict to the other
# shards. A committed batch is captured with one key post-saga and another
# absent, losing the committed write from every restore.
MODULE: BackupSagaConsistentMaskedDecisionHidden
TARGET: BackupSagaConsistent
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the gate snapshot masks an expired but recorded decision as Indeterminate
PERTURBS: GateAcquire

--- FIND
    /\ d0' = [d0 EXCEPT ![T] = [t \in Sagas |-> loc[t][T]]]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: an expired tombstone is masked as Indeterminate.
    /\ d0' = [d0 EXCEPT ![T] = [t \in Sagas |->
               IF T = "T1" /\ t = "s" /\ expired /\ loc[t][T] # "none" THEN "indeterminate" ELSE loc[t][T]]]
--- END